  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) Civilisational Dialogue, hosted in New Delhi, saw the participation of high-ranking officials including Pakistan Minister Musadik Malik. During his visit to the Purana Qila, Malik referenced historical figures such as Humayun and Sher Shah Suri to underscore the shared cultural heritage of the region. Prime Minister Narendra Modi opened the forum, emphasizing the importance of civilisational discourse over conflict. The event occurred despite significant diplomatic friction between India and Pakistan, with reports noting Pakistani requests for renewed talks contrasted against Indian concerns regarding terrorism. The forum ultimately resulted in the adoption of a formal document that recognizes culture as a foundational element for cooperation among SCO nations, acknowledging centuries of interaction while maintaining distinct national identities and traditions.",
